[openLISEM runfile version 6.0]

; SWATRE variant of tiny.run -- same 10x10 catchment, Infil Method=1
; (INFIL_SWATRE) instead of 3 (Green & Ampt/Smith & Parlange). Built to
; exercise a second, genuinely different infiltration code path: SWATRE
; solves a Richards-equation-like N-node soil column per cell (see
; swatre/swatstep.cpp) using a profile definition (profile.inp) and a soil
; moisture-retention/conductivity lookup table (loam.tbl), rather than
; Green & Ampt's simpler wetting-front approximation.
;
; SYNTHETIC, not measured: loam.tbl's theta/h(suction)/K rows are a
; hand-picked, physically-ordered (theta and K both increasing as suction
; -> 0) retention/conductivity curve in the shape a real Brooks-Corey or
; van Genuchten fit would have -- not fit to any real soil sample. The
; point is exercising SWATRE's code path with internally-consistent,
; monotonic inputs (the reader enforces strictly-increasing theta/h/K --
; see swatre/swatinp.cpp's ReadSoilTableNew), not modeling a real soil.
;
; "Use one matrix potential=1" is set so SWATRE initializes every node to
; a single user-given matric potential ("Initial matrix potential") rather
; than needing a series of inithead.NNN initial-condition maps -- avoids
; needing N more synthetic map files for a fixture that's already
; synthetic throughout.
;
; Infil Method=1 skips the entire Green & Ampt map-reading block in
; lisDataInit.cpp (guarded by `if (InfilMethod != INFIL_SWATRE)`), so this
; fixture does NOT reference ksat1.map/thetas1.map/thetai1.map/psi1.map/
; soildepth1.map at all -- SWATRE draws its soil properties entirely from
; profile.inp + loam.tbl instead.
;
; Paths are ABSOLUTE (host-specific), same convention as tiny.run/tiny3.run.

